PollRawUDPSockets (steamnetworkingsockets_lowlevel.cpp) asserts
s_hSockWakeThreadRead != INVALID_SOCKET when building its poll list --
fires every call on Emscripten, since the Init-time IsEmscripten()
branch above intentionally leaves it invalid. poll() ignores negative
fds, so the fix just reserves the slot with one instead of asserting.

wasm64 (Emscripten's MEMORY64 target) specifically, found via an actual
wasm64-emscripten CI build (native wasm32 already worked -- this is
wasm64-only): "typedef redefinition with different types ('long' vs
'long long')" in minbase_types.h, plus knock-on "constructor cannot be
redeclared" errors in steamclientpublic.h wherever it overloads on
int64/int64_t as distinct types.

Root cause: minbase_types.h's own int64_t typedef branches on
`COMPILER_GCC && PLATFORM_64BITS && ...`, assuming traditional Linux
LP64 semantics (`long` is 64-bit and IS the system's int64_t) --
correct for real GCC/Linux, wrong for Emscripten. Two things conspire:
Emscripten's clang defines __GNUC__ (for GCC-macro compatibility), so
minbase_identify.h's own COMPILER_GCC detection (`defined(__GCC__) ||
defined(__GNUC__)`) already treats it as COMPILER_GCC; and wasm64
genuinely sets PLATFORM_64BITS (real 64-bit pointers under MEMORY64).
So this branch fires for wasm64, defining int64_t as `long int` --- but
Emscripten's own <stdint.h> uses `long long` for int64_t regardless of
pointer width, causing a direct typedef conflict the instant anything
includes both. Excluded the same way the rest of this patch treats
Emscripten as its own platform identity rather than piggybacking on
Linux/GCC assumptions it doesn't actually share.

diff --git a/src/public/minbase/minbase_types.h b/src/public/minbase/minbase_types.h
--- a/src/public/minbase/minbase_types.h
+++ b/src/public/minbase/minbase_types.h
@@ -75,7 +75,7 @@
 // NOTE: int64_t must match the compiler stdint.h definition
 // and so may not match the Steam int64.  Mixing the two is
 // error-prone so always use the Steam non-_t types in Steam code.
-#if defined(COMPILER_GCC) && defined(PLATFORM_64BITS) && !defined(__MINGW32__) && !IsOSX() && !(defined(IOS) || defined(TVOS))
+#if defined(COMPILER_GCC) && defined(PLATFORM_64BITS) && !defined(__MINGW32__) && !IsOSX() && !(defined(IOS) || defined(TVOS)) && !IsEmscripten()
 #define INT64_DIFFERENT_FROM_INT64_T 1
 typedef long int int64_t;
 typedef unsigned long int uint64_t;
